The following table sets forth information regarding our non-interest expense:

For the three months ended September 30, 2026, non-interest expense increased $39.2 million, or 25.1%, primarily due to increases of:

• $20.8 million in depreciation and amortization primarily due to depreciation on equipment under operating leases following the Verdant acquisition and an increase in intangible amortization expense following the acquisition of deposits;

• $8.2 million in salaries and related costs primarily due to increased headcount and salaries, including the impact of the Verdant acquisition;

• $5.4 million in general and administrative expenses primarily reflecting higher loan and lease servicing and processing expenses following the Verdant acquisition; and

• $4.4 million in data and operational processing expenses as the Company continues to invest in technology to support its growth.

